d-solution" "value" "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nLet's start by listing all the elements of $A:$\n\n$$\n∅,\\,{∅},\\,{{∅}}\n$$\n\nNote that $∅,$ ${∅},$ and ${{∅}}$ each count as single elements of $A.$\n\nSince $A$ has $3$ elements, the cardinality is $|A|=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddf89908ec0107b12831d1b3a8e48a0c3a1c4254906029122e8849802cdd5705" "basis" 1418 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80737" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d7afcc22e495cd59a70ed0ce2418d273eae039b06861a1a5de81aae975410d20" "basis" 1418 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80737" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddf89908ec0107b12831d1b3a8e48a0c3a1c4254906029122e8849802cdd5705" "basis" 1418 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80737" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddf89908ec0107b12831d1b3a8e48a0c3a1c4254906029122e8849802cdd5