ademy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80737" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddf89908ec0107b12831d1b3a8e48a0c3a1c4254906029122e8849802cdd5705" "basis" 1418 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-181563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $A={-200,-193,-186,…,997},$ then $|A|=${{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddf89908ec0107b12831d1b3a8e48a0c3a1c4254906029122e8849802cdd5705" "basis" 1418 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-181563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nNotice that the elements of our set \n\n$$\n-200,\\,-193,\\,-186,\\,…\n$$\n\nform an arithmetic sequence with a common difference $d=7:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =7 \\\\  & =-193-(-200) \\\\  & =-186-(-193) \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our arithmetic sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =-200+(n-1)\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =-200+7n-7 \\\\  & =7n-207.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={7n-207:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le N}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7N-207 & =997 \\\\ 7N & =1\\,204 \\\\ N & =\\frac{1\\,204}{7} \\\\ N & =172\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA={7n-207:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le 172}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $172$ elements, we must have $|A|=172.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddf89908ec0107b12831d1b3a8e48a0c3a1c4254906029122e8849802cdd5705" "basis" 1418 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-181563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d7afcc22e495cd59a70ed0ce2418d273eae039b06861a1a5de81aae975410d20" "basis" 1418 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-181563" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddf89908ec0107b12831d1b3a8e48a0c3a1c4254906029122e8849802cdd5705" "basis" 1418 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-181563" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "172"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddf89908ec0107b12831d1b3a8e48a0c3a1c4254906029122e8849802cdd5705" "basis" 1418 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-181559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $A={15,21,27,…,1\\,905},$ then $|A|=${{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddf89908ec0107b12831d1b3a8e48a0c3a1c4254906029122e8849802cdd5705" "basis" 1418 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-181559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nNotice that the elements of our set \n\n$$\n15,\\,21,\\,27,\\,…\n$$\n\nform an arithmetic sequence with a common difference $d=6:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =6 \\\\  & =21-15 \\\\  & =27-21 \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our arithmetic sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =15+(n-1)\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =15+6n-6 \\\\  & =6n+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={6n+9:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le N}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6N+9 & =1\\,905 \\\\ 6N & =1\\,896 \\\\ N & =\\frac{1\\,896}{6} \\\\ N & =316\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA={6n+9:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le 316}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $316$ elements, we must have $|A|=316.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddf89908ec0107b12831d1b3a8e48a0c3a1c4254906029122e8849802cdd5705" "basis" 1418 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-181559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d7afcc22e495cd59a70ed0ce2418d273eae039b06861a1a5de81aae975410d20" "basis" 1418 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-181559" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddf89908ec0107b12831d1b3a8e48a0c3a1c4254906029122e8849802cdd5705" "basis" 1418 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-181582" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $A={1,6,36,216,…,2\\,176\\,782\\,336},$ then $|A|=${{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddf89908ec0107b12831d1b3a8e48a0c3a1c4254906029122e8849802cdd5705" "basis" 1418 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-181582" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nNotice that the elements of our set \n\n$$\n1,\\,6,\\,36,\\,216,\\,…\n$$\n\nform a geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=6:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =6 \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{6} \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our geometric sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1}=1\\cdot {6}^{n-1}={6}^{n-1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\nA={{6}^{n-1}:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le N}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{6}^{N-1} & =2\\,176\\,782\\,336 \\\\ N-1 & ={log}_{6}⁡(2\\,176\\,782\\,336) \\\\ N-1 & =\\frac{{log}_{10}⁡(2\\,176\\,782\\,336)}{{log}_{10}⁡(6)} \\\\ N-1 & =12 \\\\ N & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA={{6}^{n-1}:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le 13}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $13$ elements, we must have $|A|=13.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddf89908ec0107b12831d1b3a8e48a0c3a1c4254906029122e8849802cdd5705" "basis" 1418 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-181582" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d7afcc22e495cd59a70ed0ce2418d273eae039b06861a1a5de81aae975410d20" "basis" 1418 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-181582" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040149/state.json" "file_sha256" "ddf89908ec0107b12831d1b3a8e48a0c3a1c4254906029122e8849802cdd5705" "basis" 1418 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/