ion/worked-solution" "value" "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nNotice that the elements of our set \n\n$$\n98,\\,102,\\,106,\\,…\n$$\n\nform an arithmetic sequence with a common difference $d=4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =4 \\\\  & =102-98 \\\\  & =106-102 \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our arithmetic sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =98+(n-1)\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =98+4n-4 \\\\  & =4n+94.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $A$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={4n+94:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le N}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $N\\in N$ is to be determined.\n\nTo find $N,$ we solve the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4N+94 & =810 \\\\ 4N & =716 \\\\ N & =\\frac{716}{4} \\\\ N & =179\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\nA={4n+94:n\\in N,\\,1\\le n\\le 179}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A$ has $179$ elements, we must have $|A|=179.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071099/state.json" "file_sha256" "33ddcc82728c8b73f06200b96a9cc05ffaa6bf3c13b298466e1bca5d2a7fa3f3"} {"question" "q-181561" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071099/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3144a4334782a62050a0811e21313a4a537bc521b0680b93202a42b6753a09db"} {"question" "q-181561" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071099/state.json" "file_sha256" "33ddcc82728c8b73f06200b96a9cc05ffaa6bf3c13b298466e1bca5d2a7fa3f3"} {"question" "q-181561" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "179"] "category" "ma_successful